{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#978","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#978","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#978\",\"parent_revision\":\"379108ce641c614c98dede857812ff22f0457dd0b46fedc2eef480416adb1d18\",\"root_revision\":\"379108ce641c614c98dede857812ff22f0457dd0b46fedc2eef480416adb1d18\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nCreate a task-worker agent in development-harness that serves as the universal SAM task executor.\\n\\nThe task-worker is the amorphous any-agent. It receives a task reference (P{N}/T{M}), loads the task via sam_read, reads the skills listed in the task metadata, loads those skills, and executes the work. The orchestrator does not need to know which specialist agent to route to \u2014 the task metadata declares the skills needed.\\n\\nAgent responsibilities:\\n1. Parse task reference from prompt (P{N}/T{M} pattern)\\n2. Load task via sam_read(plan=P{N}, task=T{M}) \u2014 if this fails, report error and stop\\n3. Read the skills field from task metadata\\n4. Load each skill via Skill(skill=\\\"{name}\\\") \u2014 conditional or unconditional as instructed\\n5. Claim the task via sam_claim\\n6. Execute against acceptance criteria from the task\\n7. Run verification steps\\n8. Track progress via sam_state\\n9. Report structured completion (STATUS: COMPLETE/PARTIAL/FAILED with details)\\n\\nAgent frontmatter:\\n- name: task-worker\\n- tools: all tools\\n- mcpServers: sam, backlog (explicit declaration)\\n- skills: dh:subagent-contract (bounded specialist behavior)\\n- model: inherit (orchestrator chooses model per task complexity)\\n\\nThis agent replaces the need for the orchestrator to route tasks to specific agent types (python-cli-architect, contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer, etc.). The task file's skills field determines what the worker loads \u2014 the worker adapts to any domain by loading the right skills.\\n\\nComplements /dh:dispatch (manager guidance) \u2014 dispatch creates teams of task-workers.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **create task-worker agent \u2014 universal sam task executor that loads skills from task metadata** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-21: completing the manager/worker architecture with dispatch skill as manager guidance and task-worker as the universal worker\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f6df8a5a3b391fa9a535b3865263ad4a17e83e7494611a00cd5133ed8fbfe829\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWXvhg\"}"}